{{Quote|You will never stop us. We will not be broken. However long it takes, we will never stop fighting.|Caluan Ematt, to Commander Alecia Beck|<ref name="Smuggler's Run" />}}
'''Caluan Ematt''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[soldier]] who served as a [[lieutenant]] in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. He fought against the [[Galactic Empire]], during which Ematt was given [[Commander|command]] of the [[Shrikes]], a special recon unit that was tasked with identifying, securing and preparing new Rebel bases for the Alliance. He was a friend of [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] and would later go on to serve with her at a [[Resistance base]] as a [[major]], and later [[general]] in the [[Resistance]] during the [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] against the [[First Order]].

==Biography==
===Early life===
Caluan Ematt was [[Reproduction|born]] on the industrial [[Core Worlds|Core World]] [[Champat]] in [[20 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines" />

===Galactic Civil War===
====Leader of the Shrikes====
[[File:Lt_Ematt.jpg|thumb|left|Ematt as a lieutenant]]
[[Lieutenant]] Caluan Ematt was a [[Rebel trooper|soldier]] in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during its fight against the [[Galactic Empire]] in the [[Galactic Civil War]] serving as part of the [[Shrikes]] recon unit.<ref name="Smuggler's Run" />

====Scouting for the Alliance====
Ematt was leading a six person team scouting for potential bases for the Rebel Alliance. They were on [[Taanab]] when they were ambushed by an [[Imperial Security Bureau]] force led by [[Alecia Beck]]. He managed to escape the ambush and sent a burst transmission to the [[Alliance High Command]] informing them of his plan to hide in the city of [[Motok]] on [[Cyrkon]]. He stowed away on a [[Kuat Drive Yards|Kuat Yards]] hauler in a freight container. Once on Motok, he visited a [[Unidentified cantina (Motok)|cantina]] but left without talking to anyone. Ematt hid out in a hotel on the outskirts of Motok, but let [[Delia Leighton]] know he was looking for a way off-planet.<ref name="SR">''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Run]]''</ref>

[[Han Solo]] and his co-pilot [[Chewbacca]] were tasked by [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] to meet Ematt and get him to safety before he could be captured and interrogated. She knew that Ematt held vast amounts of data on the Rebellion's plans, future bases, and supply caches and if the Empire could extract that from the soldier, it could mean the end of the war. The smugglers flew to Cyrkon and located Ematt. After receiving the pass-phrase, he let them into his room and prepared to depart. Before they could leave, the environmental alarms in the building went off, which was a signal that Solo had arranged with a local bum in case of trouble. Ematt suggested that they escape down the stairs, but they were locked due to the alarms.<ref name="SR" />

As Chewbacca tried to hotwire the door, a group of bounty hunters exited the elevators and opened fire on Ematt and the smugglers. The Wookiee forced the door open and the trio fled down the stairs to the [[V-40]] [[landspeeder]] Solo had rented. The group made their way to the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' but before they could board they were ambushed by Beck and a group of [[Stormtrooper]]s. Ematt boarded the ''Falcon'' after Solo and Chewbacca created a distraction with the aid of the ''[[Serendipity|Miss Fortune]]''. The two ships then fled the planet but were intercepted by the ''[[Vehement]]'' who sent [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE fighters]] to attack the two [[Starship|ships]].<ref name="SR" />

Ematt took control of the ''Falcon''{{'s}} [[quad laser cannon]]s and proceeded to shoot down several fighters. He entered the coordinates for the rendezvous with the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Rebel fleet]] into the ''Falcon''{{'s}} [[Navigation computer|navicomputer]] but Solo refused to leave the damaged ''Miss Fortune'' alone against the Imperials. When the freighter was captured by a [[tractor beam]] from the ''Vehement'', Ematt vowed that he would not be taken alive. Solo assured him that they would escape, and managed to elude the [[Star Destroyer]] by diving toward the planet's surface until the tractor beam lost contact.<ref name="SR" />

====Mission to the ''Graceful Promising''====
At some point after the [[Battle of Yavin]], Ematt was requested by Han Solo to aid in a [[Mission to the Graceful Promising|scavenging operation]] to the ''[[Graceful Promising]]'', a derelict Vontorian treasure ship. The ship had been loaded with treasures by the famed pirate queen [[Maz Kanata]] and had since then been locked into close orbit around a dark star. Accompanied by several Alliance Pathfinders, Ematt worked in concert with Solo and Chewbacca which resulted in a successful mission. Among one of the many useful finds was a significant batch of [[Kiirium]]. Solo then decided to let the Alliance keep most of the money gained from the mission despite his debts to Jabba.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]''</ref>

====Zastiga====
Shortly after the [[Battle of Hoth]], Ematt accompanied [[Nien Nunb]] to the ''[[Remembrance]]'' so that they could pick Leia Organa up and take her to a secret meeting with the leadership of the Alliance to Restore the Republic on [[Zastiga]].<ref name="Moving Target" />

====Sullust====
{{Quote|I went to Sullust during the late stages of the siege to assist the native resistance. As I recall, Twilight Company already had the situation well in hand.|Caluan Ematt|<ref name="Rebel Files" />}}
After the stalling of [[Operation Ringbreaker]]<ref name="Rebel Files" /> in [[3 ABY]],<ref name="Date">The section of ''[[Battlefront: Twilight Company]]'' where Vixus [[Squadron]] appears takes place is set twenty-two [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Clone Wars]], which [[Mission to Mustafar|ended]] in [[19 BBY]], according to ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''. Vixus Squadron must have therefore appeared in [[3 ABY]].</ref> Ematt traveled to the planet [[Sullust]] to help the [[Sullustan Resistance]] during<ref name="Rebel Files" /> the Empire's [[Siege of Inyusu Tor|siege]] on the Alliance's [[61st Mobile Infantry]], better known as Twilight Company, at the [[Inyusu Tor mineral processing facility]].<ref name="BTC">''[[Battlefront: Twilight Company]]''</ref>

====Battle of Endor====
Ematt was later part of the [[Endor strike team]] led by [[General]] Han Solo, and participated in the climactic [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="Rebel Files" />

===Joining the Resistance===
<div style="float: right">[[File:Major_Ematt_edit.png|thumb|right|200px|Ematt as a Resistance major]]</div>
Eventually the Alliance to Restore the Republic was able to defeat the Empire and formed the [[New Republic]], with Ematt becoming a member.<ref name="Bloodline" /> In [[28 ABY]],<ref name="Timeframe">{{Twitter|DelReyStarWars|status/652893780236988420|[[Del Rey]]|quote=So excited to have @claudiagray writing a #StarWars novel with us. SW: New Republic: Bloodline coming 2016. Set 6 years before TFA.|archivefile=File:New Republic Bloodline Twitter Post.jpg}} establishes that the events of [[Bloodline (novel)|''Bloodline'']] take place six [[Standard year|years]] before the events of {{Film|VII}}. ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of ''The Force Awakens'' to [[34 ABY]], so ''Bloodline'' must take place in [[28 ABY]].</ref> following the [[Tai-Lin Garr's assassination|assassination]] of [[Senator]] [[Tai-Lin Garr]], Ematt attended a secret meeting with several other [[New Republic soldier]]s, [[pilot]]s, and [[officer]]s where Leia announced the formation of the [[Resistance]], a paramilitary organization dedicated to defending the New Republic from threats like the [[First Order]].<ref name="Bloodline" />

In the early [[Standard day|days]] of the Resistance, Ematt served as an [[agent]] for Organa by continuing his service in the [[New Republic Defense Force]] whilst seeking potential converts for the Resistance. After the defection of too many [[New Republic pilot]]s to go unnoticed, Ematt left his post in the Republic to fully join the Resistance.<ref name="ECUC" />

====Recruiting Poe Dameron====
In [[31 ABY]],<ref name="BTA date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' states that [[BB-8]] and [[Poe Dameron]] joined the [[Resistance]] three [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Hosnian Cataclysm|Starkiller Incident]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[34 ABY]]. Therefore, BB-8 and Dameron joined the Resistance in [[31 ABY]].</ref> he escorted Organa to the [[Mirrin Prime Republic base]] to see the recruitment of [[Commander]] [[Poe Dameron]], fresh from a [[Skirmish in OR-Kappa-2722|skirmish]] with the First Order. Ematt intercepted the young pilot as he landed with two [[shore police]], and brought him to Organa.<ref name="Before">''[[Before the Awakening]]''</ref>

====Battle of Crait====
{{Quote|Ground forces, incoming.|Caluan Ematt during the Battle of Crait|<ref name="Episode VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>}}
[[File:EmattOnCrait-TheLastJedi5.jpg|thumb|right|200px|General Ematt with his troops on Crait.]]
Following the [[Battle of Starkiller Base]], Ematt was promoted from [[major]] to general.<ref name="Visual Dictionary">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> During the [[Battle of Crait]], Ematt observed the [[All Terrain MegaCaliber Six|AT-M6s]] and [[First Order All Terrain Armored Transport|AT-ATs]] en route to [[Crait outpost]], and was situated near a trench while his men took positions.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Trust is as precious as it is rare, but you only get it by giving it.|Caluan Ematt, to Han Solo|<ref name="Smuggler's Run" />}}
Caluan Ematt was a [[human]] male with [[Color|brown]] hair and [[eye]]s.<ref name="Smuggler's Run" />

==Behind the scenes==
Caluan Ematt first appeared in the simultaneous release of ''[[Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo & Chewbacca Adventure]]'' and ''[[Moving Target: A Princess Leia Adventure]]'' on [[Force Friday]] in [[2015]], identified only as "Ematt." Later that [[September]], [[Wikipedia:Nestlé|Nestlé]] released [[Smuggler's Run (animated comic)|''Smuggler's Run'']], an animated adaptation of the novel, in which Ematt's first name is identified as "Caluan." [[Jordan D. White]], an editor for the ''[[Star Wars]]'' comics at [[Marvel Comics|Marvel]] who worked on the video, confirmed the spelling on [https://twitter.com/cracksh0t/status/649295573229654016 Twitter]. He was portrayed by [[Andrew Jack]] in [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']] and [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']].

Ematt appears in concept art for the [[Resistance base (Ajan Kloss)|Resistance base]] in [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']],<ref name="Art of TROS">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker]]''</ref> but is not in the movie itself.<ref name="TROS">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

